{
    "background_story": "Jream was a renowned architect known for his innovative and ambitious designs. His latest project, the Aurora Tower, was a marvel of engineering that seemed to defy gravity. However, as the construction progressed, Jream became increasingly obsessed with adding more features, more flourishes, and more complexity. His team struggled to keep up with his ever-changing vision, and the project's timeline and budget began to spiral out of control. Despite the warnings from his colleagues, Jream couldn't resist the urge to add just one more element, one more detail. The Aurora Tower became a symbol of his unyielding passion, but also a testament to the dangers of being superincumbent - piling on too much, too fast, and risking collapse under the weight of one's own ambition.",
